    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2e8c30a_139d1e5e",
        "filename": "compos/composd/src/instance_manager.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T15:46:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I defined the ART property unsigned, and the vendor one signed. (That\u0027s why the read property fn is generified - there\u0027s 2 types.)\nI want to allow maximum flexibility there, and at least in theory they might have lower overhead than Microdroid. (Although \"caveat vendor\".)",
      "parentUuid": "32e10257_6d19824a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "8d35160ef501726be947750890129b2f551787a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afdecc1f_0cae6f25",
        "filename": "compos/composd/src/instance_manager.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T16:33:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then are we still going to have a \"balloon test\" up to `composd.vm.art.memory_mib.config`? If we can\u0027t guarantee ART can use that amount of memory across the boards, the monitoring during a Mainline rollout will be more important.\n\nCan we ask vendors to contribute microdroid improvement back to AOSP? Especially if we still want to make it a Mainline module in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "c2e8c30a_139d1e5e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "8d35160ef501726be947750890129b2f551787a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eae1c033_605a16d7",
        "filename": "compos/composd/src/instance_manager.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T16:44:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I shouldn\u0027t have called out Microdroid specifically - I just assume different hypervisors might lead to different levels of overhead.\n\nI think careful monitoring is going to be necessary anyway - if the vendor sets it to 10, but they should have set it to 20, then problems could arise, just as if they were to erroneously set it to -10.\n\nI think we\u0027ll need to make it clear they need to be very careful.",
      "parentUuid": "afdecc1f_0cae6f25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "8d35160ef501726be947750890129b2f551787a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c994724_55ae1d73",
        "filename": "compos/composd/src/instance_manager.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-24T16:54:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SGTM.  Ideally, we would separate ART, Microdroid usage and vendor adjustment.  We would guarantee ART can get what they need by 1) a restriction of -(vendor adjustment) \u003c\u003d Microdroid usage, and 2) ballooning to ART\u0027s request can always succeed.  But I\u0027m not sure how feasible it is, and like you said, we should monitor the rollout anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "eae1c033_605a16d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 27
      },
